-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


.

  Hello all,

  This is to announce the release of xisp version 1.6, an X11 visual
 interface to pppd/chat, in other words, an X11 dialup networking
 tool for Linux. The .lsm entry and part of the README file is included
 below. Everything is in sunsite.unc.edu:/incoming/Linux right now but
 it should appear in its proper location shortly.

  Changes from version 1.5 include: enhancement of the modem options
 form - now termed communication options - which also now includes
 modem device and speed, and compression options, plus some bug-fixes.
 Since changes were made to the .xisprc file format, xisprccv now
 converts your .xisprc to v1.6 format; just run the xisprccv utility
 with no arguments. Note also that an alternative site has been added
 to the .lsm entry; depending on where you are it might be easier to
 get xisp from there instead of sunsite.

 Please send bug reports/enhancements/suggestions to dbouras@hol.gr.
 With greetings from sunny Athens, Greece,

  Dimitri

