Hi there, 
I am looking for volunteers who like to play with bras, which
is my replacement of `make' written in Tcl and meant to cure some of the
misfeatures of make, like

	the crazy syntax (tabs as a structuring element!),
	the way variables are expanded,
	the inability to handle dependencies in foreign directories,
	the inability to distinguish between targets that merely need to
	  exist and those that must be newer than their dependencies,
	the lack of file-targets which always must be build,
	the lack of control structures and 
	the lack of decent pattern matching.

At 
	http://www.iitb.fhg.de/~kir/
you find a paragraph on bras with links for downloading and reading the
on-line docu.

Have fun and tell me what you think.

