-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I have released dhcpcd-0.6. The following lists all the bug
fixes and new features added in this release:

   1. fixed the bug that the renewal time and the rebind time
      are messed up (becomes minus number :p) when dhcpcd gets
      the lease time whose least significant byte is greater
      than or equal to 0x80. For example, dhcpcd does not work
      if the lease time is 24 hours.
   2. added the hostname option to the parameter request list
   3. fixed the bug that dhcpcd sends a DHCPREQUEST message
      which does not have the server identifier option when it
      is in the SELECTING state.
   4. fixed the bug that dhcpcd uses the information from the
      DHCPOFFER message for configuring the host (it must use
      the information from the DHCPREQUEST message)
   5. fixed the bug that DHCPDECLINE message was RFC1541
      compliant. Now dhcpcd can send both Interned Draft
      compliant DHCPDECLINE message and RFC1541 compliant
      one.
   6. fixed the bug that the broadcast address and the subnetmask
      were set to the wrong value under the following condition:
	1. dhcpcd is in the REBOOTING state
	2. received DHCPACK message does not include the
	   broadcast or subnetmask option.
   7. fixed the bug that dhcpcd does not send a DHCPDECLINE
      message when it detects a duplicate IP adddresse
   8. changed the way to make a DHCPREQUEST message in the
      SELECTING state.
   9. changed the pcmcia/network script to unmount the NFS
      filesystems before invoking "dhcpcd -k" command when
      the card service goes down.
  10. added a new environment variable DHCP_DEVICE, which
      contains the name of network interface to which dhcpcd is
      attached.


The following is its LSM file:

Begin3
Title:          dhcpcd
Version:        0.6
Entered-date:   20MAR97
Description:    dhcpcd is an Internet Draft and RFC1541 compliant DHCP
                client daemon. It gets an IP address and other
                information from a corresponding DHCP server,
                configures the network interface automatically, and
                tries to renew the lease time according to
                draft-ietf-dhc-dhcp-09. By default, dhcpcd 0.6 works
                in the Internet Draft compliant mode. It works in the
                RFC1541 compliant mode when the '-r' option is specified.
                So far it is found that dhcpcd 0.6 works fine with the
                following DHCP servers:
                  1. ISC's dhcpcd-BETA-5.14
                  2. DHCP server on Windows NT server 3.51
                  3. DHCP server version 1.3b by WIDE project.
                See the "Changes" file if you want to know the difference
                from the previous version.
