-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Announcing the first pre-release of the Astonishing Figurine, version 0.0.0!


Why Figurine?
- -------------

My impression of Unix programmers (in particular, the developers of free
systems like Linux) is that they have little time to worry about user
friendliness.  Let's face it, given the choice between "more features" and
"ease of use" any self-respecting Unix programmer will always choose "more
features."

And that's exactly the way it should be!  There are enough systems out there
that concentrate on the user interface to the exclusion of useful features,
and Unix doesn't need to become another one.  However, there's no reason
that we can't try to make Unix systems easier to use, without bothering the
other "Real Programmers" out there.


Introducing the Configuration Modeller
- --------------------------------------

Figurine is what I call a "configuration modeller."  The main idea is
that a Real Programmer can set up a software _model_ of a package's
configuration files, without worrying how this model will be presented to
the user.  The model is completely separate from the user interface.

figurine does the dirty work of presenting this model to the user.  This has
two main advantages:

- - The person who creates the model does not have to care about or know about
  user interface design;

- - figurine can present different user interfaces depending on the user's
  preference and the availability of a windowing system.
		
Right now the second advantage is rather silly since this version of
figurine only has the one interface module available.


You Can Help!
- -------------
	
The figurine project really needs _your_ input and ideas!  You don't need to
be a programmer to give advice about the user interface and features you
would like to see.

And naturally, programmers (especially ones with lots of free time) are more
than welcome too.


Go Get it Now!
- --------------

Everyone is invited to the grand opening of the figurine Web page at:
	http://www.foxnet.net/~apenwarr/figurine/

The program is available there, along with lots of useful information.

You can join the figurine-users mailing list by sending a message with the
subject "subscribe" (do not include the quotes) to:
	figurine-users-request@lists.foxnet.net
	
And remember, don't let the 0.0.0 version number scare you.  It only means
that nobody at all has tested the system, ever.  Even my roommate has
received only fleeting glimpses of the "Astonishing" release.  Heck, _I_
don't even know if it's working half the time.

So download it today!




