-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


I've written some small utilities. They are nothing special but my be
someone will use them.

'fsplit' is a utilitie to split larger binary files into several smaller
files. Each part will fitt on a floppy disk. The size of the parts is
selectable on command line. 'fsplit' stores some thisngs like permissions,
date and time of the original file in a header on the beginning of each
part.
'fmerge' is the opposite of 'fsplit'. It merges the previously splitted
parts together. It uses the stored information in the header of each part
to set the permissions (if possible), date and time of the file. 'fmerge'
can merge all files by simly giving the original file name as a parameter
to it. Nothing else is required.

The utilities are available from:

   http://members.ping.at/theofilu/fsplit.tar.gz

The utilities are not under GPL currently, but are mostly free for private
and commercial use. Please read the license file, included in the
TAR-archive.


