ANNOUNCEMENT: GLCHESS-0.10alpha
- -------------------------------

GLchess is a frontend to the GNUchess. It's on the alpha stage, which
means it's probably buggy and surely unoptimized, but mainly fulfills
it's job, which is to look pretty. Most of the playability and options
of gnuchess are not (yet) implemented, and I welcome all bugfixes,
patches and rewrites you want to send me.

If you have just installed Your First Linux(tm), don't bother to take
this, because it prolly won't compile in a snap. I've managed to compile
this with Linux and Mesa, with IRIX 5.3 and 6.2 with GL and Mesa, and
with Digital Unix 4.0 (it segfaulted later, but I've successfully run it
on DEC Alpha over X, and boy, it was unbelievable fast =)

GLchess needs gnuchess-4.0 (pl77 tested), Mesa-2.1, and OpenGL-library if
you have one on your platform. If you have native GL-libraries (like SGI
and DEC Alpha), you still need libMesatk. If you don't have real GL-libs,
don't worry, MesaGL works out fine.

You can read details, check screenshots and fetch it from
http://nether.tky.hut.fi/glchess/

Thank you for your attention.

- --
