		     The Third Annual Linux Expo
			  April 4th and 5th
		 North Carolina Biotechnology Center
		      Research Triangle Park, NC
		       http://www.linuxexpo.org

The 3rd Annual Linux Expo is almost here, and space is filling up fast!
With 18 technical talks by Linux developers and experts, a full day Linux
Install Fair, exhibits from 15 leading Linux companies, food and juggling,
this year's Expo will be one you don't want to miss!

Due to unprecedented demand, we've added two tents outside the Biotech
center to hold additional seating and monitors broadcasting the talks,
the food court and Linux Expo store, jugglers and other events.

TECHNICAL TALKS

The number of seats actually in the speaker auditorium is *very* limited
and they are nearly all sold.  If you want to get inside the auditorium
you *must* reserve your seat today.  Visit http://www.linuxexpo.org for
registration details and the complete list of speakers and talks.

INSTALL FAIR

The Linux installation fair, to be held on Saturday throughout the show,
is also filling up.  If you'd like to bring a machine and install Linux
on it at the install fair, you need to register in advance on our web site.

THE LINUX EXPO STORE

The Linux Expo Store will have its grand opening a the Expo, offering
t-shirts, bumper stickers, proceedings, and Linux books and CD-ROMs.
Soon some of these items will be available for purchase on our web site.

THE LINUX BOWL

We will be holding the First Annual Linux Bowl at the end of the Expo
on Saturday.  The Linux Bowl is patterned after the familiar quiz-show
type games, including the famous Computer Bowl held every year at the
Computer Museum.  Two teams of panelists will put their Linux
knowledge to the test answering Linux Trivia questions. Best of all
you can participate by submitting questions on our web site, and from
the audience just before the show!

Don't wait!  Register now for the greatest Linux Expo ever!

