MIME++ is a C++ class library for parsing, creating, or modifying messages in 
MIME format.  (MIME is Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions).  MIME++ includes
classes that greatly simplify the development of email, news, or HTTP applications.

My original idea for MIME++ was to create a class for every element of the BNF
grammar in the RFCs.  That idea has worked quite well.  I feel this approach
makes using the library really intuitive.  I have also created some higher level
classes, such as MultipartMessage and MessageWithAttachments, that are even
easier to use.

The latest version, 0.8.0, has been uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu at 
/pub/Linux/Incoming; it will soon be moved to /pub/Linux/devel/lang/c++/.
The most recent version is available from the MIME++ Home Page at

    http://www.fwb.gulf.net/~dwsauder/mimepp.html

This new version includes various enhancements, including HTML man pages.  For a
quick overview of the package, you can view the man pages online from the MIME++
Home Page.

- -- Doug Sauder




