mem_test helps you find the memory leaks that can result in a C
program when you allocate memory and don't free it (amazingly easy to
do even when trying to be careful). It does not look for illegal
memory access, for that I suggest Bruce Peren's Electric Fence, which
may be used in conjunction with mem_test.

mem_test consists of three basic components, a header file to include
in the program being tested, a library to link with, and a program to
analyze the log file that is created when the program is executed.

Perhaps I should make a "yet another" joke, this is certainly not the
only first ever written for this purpose. But it is the one I wrote
for my own use, and I felt that it might be useful to others.

mem_test is known to work under Linux (of course!), SunOS 4.1.2 and
HPUX 9.05.

You can get mem_test v0.10 at:

http://www.iquest.net/~jbuchana/computer.html


