available for general use.  It has many new features, and the main
ones are:

	* Support for generating images of multi-session cdroms.
	* Support for generating images of bootable cdroms using
	  the El-Torito standard.

	The package can be found on tsx-11.mit.edu in
pub/linux/packages/mkisofs, and of course any related mirror sites.

	Mkisofs is a premastering program designed to generate the raw
image of an iso9660 filessytem from a Unix file tree, and includes
support for Rock Ridge extensions.  Mkisofs itself doesn't actually
burn the cdrom or talk to the cd writer - you need a seperate program
(such as cdwrite) to accomplish this task.  A result of this is that
mkisofs itself is quite platform independent and should work on nearly
any Unix platform.





