 PRODOSEMU = EMULATION OF APPLE II ON UNIX!!!
=============================================
 
Welcome to the Big Apple Users Group, a computer club for users of Apple
II and compatible computers. 
 
On Monday, March 24, at 6:30 pm, the Apple II SIG will meet at 345 West
58th Street, Apt 5L, Manhattan, NYC, next to the Coliseum, just west of
Columbus Circle.  Bill Katz will present Prodosemu, an Apple II ProDos
emulation program which runs on Unix.  Bill has tweaked it so that it runs
on 3 varieties of Unix.  (I believe they were Linux, Free SCO, and SunOS. 
I don't know which version Bill plans to demo.) Come and see AppleWorks
and other Apple II programs on Unix!  This demo should broaden our concept
of an Apple II compatible computer. 
 
You can also find out everything you wanted to know about the Apple II but
were afraid to ask about during the question and answer period.  You can
ask any questions you may have, or make any statement or announcement of
interest to Apple II users. 
 
We will take a short break after the Q&A session and before we get to the
Unix demo.  You can socialize or talk to other members or friends about
questions raised in the Q&A session, or other matters which concern you. 
 
The Trenton Computer Fair will take place this year on the weekend of
April 26 and 27, at the Mercer County Community College, in New Jersey. 
Apple II users will be interested mainly in the flea market, in the
parking lot out back, where vendors sell old equipment, software, and
books.  There are a few vendors who have old Apple II products to sell. 
Caveat emptor!  (Let the buyer beware!) Of course, anyone looking for a
good deal will have shove Hank and me aside.  The New York Amateur
Computer Club is running a bus on Saturday, April 26, which leaves at 8 am
from 6th Ave. (Avenida de las Americas) and 11th Street.  We will let you
know as we find out more about TCF. 
 
We try to keep these notices posted on the comp.sys.apple2.usergroups and
dorsai.chat newsgroups.  You may also call our hotline at (212)606-2297
for our latest meeting notice.  If you have any questions you may call us
at (718)499-7470 or (212)956-3634, or send us e-mail at baug@dorsai.org. 
 
We hope to see you in the near future.  You are welcome whether you are a
novice or a power user.


