-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


- -----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Quite a few people have been asking about ISODE and LDAP for Linux. Here
goes:

- - -----

ISODE is the ISO Development Environment for the OSI networking layers. 
The package includes the headers, static libraries, various development
utils, and documentation for the last freely available version,
ISODE-8.0pl1. No shared libraries, no SNMP support, and untested. Some
generous soul could always offer to maintain this pile of bureaucratic
junk which I had the misfortune of taking on.

Currently at ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/incoming/, soon to move to
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/contrib/RPMS/isode-8.0-1.i386.rpm and
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/contrib/SRPMS/isode-8.0-1.src.rpm

- - -----

LDAP is the Lightweight Directory Access Protocol. This is the UofMich
freely available implementation. The package include the standalone LDAP
server, the replication server, the LDAP <-> X.500 gateway, LDAP database
manipulation utils, and various LDAP clients. The -devel package has the
header files and static libraries needed to develop programs that use
LDAP. Maintainer wanted for this too.

Currently at ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/incoming, soon to move to
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/contrib/RPMS/ldap-3.3-1.i386.rpm,
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/contrib/RPMS/ldap-devel-3.3-1.i386.rpm, and
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/contrib/SRPMS/ldap-3.3-1.src.rpm

Sorry, but I don't feel like putting up tarballs of these. If you don't
have RPM, and want to use the software contained in these packages, get
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/redhat/code/rpm/rpm-2.3.x/rpm-2.3.2-1.i386.tar.gz
and run the rpm2cpio binary contained therein to convert the source or
binary rpms to cpio archives.

Hope this helps,
- - -- Elliot Lee
