-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Announcing the first release of YADE - Yet Another Diagram Editor.

The software provides a base system for editing different kind of
diagrams. It provides simple user interface and a framework for attaching
selfmade diagram specifications to the system. 

Originally the software was intended for making various software
engineering diagrams(like OMT, UML etc..), but because of it's
modularity and extensibility it is possible to build support for any
kind of diagrams. Current version does not have complete diagram type
specifications, but there are a few for testing purposes only. 

This release is not intended for people who need complete diagram
types.  This release is intended more for people who have needs for
specific diagram types or are unsatisfied with existing ones and can
do some coding.

 o Simple user interface
 o Embedded python language interpreter for extensions
 o Simple framework for diagram type specifications
 o Extensive documentation

For testing purposes and as an example, there are diagram type
specifications in the package for data flow diagrams and partial
implementation of OMT-style class diagrams.

The software should run on all Unix platforms. Supported platforms are
limited to Linux and Solaris/SunOS. Compiling YADE requires the
existance of Python1.3 or higher and Qt1.1 or higher. YADE is
currently only distributed in source format.

YADE is distributed under GNU General Public License.

The software is available at:

	http://www.iki.fi/~terop/yade.html

