I have created a patch to swapd and the Linux kernel to make them
communicate via the kernel IPC channel (like kerneld).  That's the
only way to make sure a memory request won't be denied if it can
possibly be satisfied (by adding more swap).

The LSM entry is appended below.  Note that as of now, I have had no
luck with uploading to sunsite --- they seem to be having an admin
problem there.  For now use the secondary site.  Enjoy, and do write
me if you get this accepted into the kernel distribution (I will try
myself, as well, but not too hard).

