Greetings to all.


I am now releasing the first public beta of my POP3 proxy, called
"pop3gwd", to the public. This program is designed to allow mail
retrieval from POP3 servers by systems that either:

(a) are behind a firewall or screening router OR
(b) do not have an assigned IP number OR
(c) must share a SLIP/PPP connection on another system


The pop3gwd program is free software, released under the Gnu GPL, and
is available in three different packages: RPM, SRPM and tar.gz

You may get it at the following URLs:

RPM:
http://www.cs.unibo.it/~borgia/homepage/Software/pop3gwd-0.99beta-1.i386.rpm

SRPM:
http://www.cs.unibo.it/~borgia/homepage/Software/pop3gwd-0.99beta-1.src.rpm

tar.gz:
http://www.cs.unibo.it/~borgia/homepage/Software/pop3gwd-0.99beta.tar.gz


I'm particularly interested in hearing from people running Linux on
platforms other than Intel, for I believe my program is quite
portable, but haven't had a chance to test it.

Please read the included documentation before using.

