Hi,

tkInfo is a browser for documentation in the GNU info hypertext
format. It needs Tcl 7.0 and Tk 4.0 or better and runs on Unix/X,
MacOS, and Windows.

It is available from

       http://www.math.ucsb.edu/%7Eboldt/tkinfo/

The following has changed since version 0.8 which was the last version
I announced:

  - The 'm' and 'f' commands have been implemented, allowing for 
    mouseless usage
  - better support for multiple info directories
  - colors, fonts, geometry now customizable via .Xdefaults options
  - can understand XEmacs-style menu syntax
  - now works under Windows
  - now distributed as a single tcl script
  - various minor improvements to the interface and bug fixes.  


Regards,
  Axel

