-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Yet another version of a utility to print documents 2
pages to a sheet has been completed. My version of
laserprt will print single pages, booklets and double
sided sheets (for the equivalent of 4 pages per sheet).
You need a HP compatible printer for this to work (It
might work on an inkjet...please let me know).

This does NOT need or use postscript. Instead it uses
the small type face available on all lasers. It
handles troff-style documents which do backspacing and
bolding with backspace sequences.

I use this all the time to print out docs, mail
messages, man pages, etc. I'm sure that you will find
it useful too. To get the lastest version, just set your
browser to my home page <http://www2.awinc.com/users/bvdpoel>
and download away. The 17K archive contains the
complete source, makefile, pre-compiled binary and a man page.

VERSION 1.3 is now available. Adds a few options, fixes some
bugs and can be compiled for use with A4 paper.

