amp - Audio Mpeg Player
- -----------------------

I am releasing an early version (0.7) of my mpeg audio player.
It has the following features:

- - decodes MPEG1 and MPEG2 audio streams (except for the MPEG2
  multichannel extensions). Only layer3 is supported in this
  early release. It is roughly 30% slower than the FhG/IIS
  decoder (l3dec), for now...

- - playing support for Linux & Solaris that is a little
  sketchy at this moment

- - source code is included - there is in fact no binary 
  distribution for now. It comes under a license that is
  more restrictive than GNU GPL, but it's still free.

this program was developed under Linux, and was tested on
Solaris 2.5 as well. The availability of source code should
guarantee it being ported to other platforms soon.


the main site for amp is:

   ftp://ftp.rasip.fer.hr/pub/mpeg/amp-0.7.0.tgz

If you have trouble getting amp from this site, please e-mail to
me about it.

I have also uploaded it to sunsite (sunsite.unc.edu), with a
desired location of:

	ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/multimedia/mp3/amp-0.7.0.tgz


alternatively, you can obtain the package by placing the text

   send mpeg_audio_source

in the body of your e-mail to multimedia@rasip.fer.hr


thank you,

Tomislav Uzelac
<tuzelac@rasip.fer.hr>



