Vile 7.0 - (VI-Like-Emacs)

Vile is a text editor which is extremely compatible with vi in terms of
"finger feel".  In addition, it has extended capabilities in many areas,
notably multi-file editing and viewing, key rebinding, and real X window
system support.

- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
I've just put vile 7.0 up for ftp at the usual place:

	ftp://ftp.clark.net/pub/dickey/vile/vile-7.0.tgz

and it should be mirrored soon at

        ftp://id.wing.net/pub/pgf/vile/vile-7.0.tgz

the PC binaries will appear soon, time permitting.  (I've built the OS/2
binary; other people have been building the DOS & WinNT binaries).

for those that are new around here, don't be put off or excited by the
'7' in "7.0".  it just means it's the first release of 1997.

Highlights since 6.0:

	+ lots of bug fixes, of course

	+ modify configure script to ensure that cached information is used
	  only on the system/version that was used to extract the data.

	+ add new directive "~elseif" (exec.c)

	+ allow continuation-lines in macros, denoted by a backslash at the
	  end of the line.

	+ improved color support for the termcap driver, including making it
	  work with terminfo interfaces.

	+ revived support for 'crypt' mode.

	+ implement regular-expressions in tags.

	+ work-around Linux bug that causes 'getchar()' to return incorrect
	  value after an interrupt, so inserts of ^C would be garbled (input.c).

	+ added "print-prefixed-lines-til" command to print into [p-lines]
	  while prefixing the lines with filename and line-number.

	+ modify select/paste behavior in xvile so that the default pastes text
	  at the last cursor (or mouse-click) position before selecting

	+ modify logic that forms buffer names so that shell commands will
	  be bracketed, thus avoiding an ambiguity.

	+ modify filename completion to allow completion of "." and ".." as
	  non-directory leaves.

	+ corrected OS/2 pipe problem, by closing dup'd file descriptors


