This is to announce the release of a freeware tool for measuring
software product metrics on C/C++ source code.  The tool is called CCCC,
and this release is version 2.0.3 (version 1.0 was released in November
1995, and has been in use at a small number of sites since that time).

The metrics measured include lines of code, lines of comment, McCabe's
cyclomatic complexity, and module fan-in and fan-out counts.  The
metrics are presented in the form of a report in HTML which has a table
summarizing  the results for a project as a whole, and four more which
give different levels of detail on the metrics calculated.

The tool is released in source code form, with precompiled binaries for
Linux and DOS/Win platforms.  It is based on Dr T J Parr's PCCTS
compiler generation toolkit (version 1.33), and is intended to be
modifiable and extendable.

For further details, please visit the project home page at

	http://www.fste.cowan.ac.edu.au/~tlittlef

This page contains all you need including copies of sample reports 
generated by the tool, links to download it, a little background
information on the metrics calculated, and links to a number of other
sites with information on metrics.


Hope to see you there soon.

