DFM - The Desktop-File-Manager for X11
======================================

Version alpha-1

DFM is a desktopmanager for linux and other UNIX-OS. Files are shown
as icons and every folder has it's own window. The desktopbackground
(like the rootwindow) is a special folder in the homedirectory.

Here are the current features:

- - icons may have any size and position
- - show XVPICS as icons
- - every file has it's own shell-command (activated by double click or
  drop on the icon)
- - every DFM-window has it's own background
- - copy, move, link, delete, ...
- - detail view (without icons)
- - iconname to cutbuffer (paste to xterm, ...)
- - sort icons
- - ...

TO DO (help not needed)
- - fill many functions in the contextmenu
- - change icon and shellcommand (now default and not changeable)
- - change background (")
- - fileoperations like change name, date and owners
- - create own XVPICS
- - save icon and window positions while ending DFM
- - arrange icons in a raster
- - "Constant position" icons that cannot be moved (or arranged)
- - documentation
- - structure view
- - update automatically
- - speed
- - bugs
- - ...

You need

   gcc, xforms, libXpm, libXext, X11, 16MB and a windowmanager

Available from:
http://www-c.informatik.uni-hannover.de/~kaiser/dfm/dfm.html ca. 85 KByte

Have fun and keep care: NO WARRANTY

You may distribute under the terms of the GNU General Public License
as specified in the COPYING file.

