        Computer Science House at Rochester Institute of Technology
                   Presents an Operating Systems Seminar
                 Wednesday evening (March 12th) at 8:00PM

                                   Week 12:

        Why the Phrase "strcmp() and other system calls" Annoys Me:
                 An Overview of How Operating Systems Work

                       Host: Pat Fleckenstein, Xerox

- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
           Attendance is free of charge and is open to the public
                        Refreshments will be served.
- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Abstract:
             I cannot count the number of times I have heard the
        phrase "plugh and other system calls" where "plugh" is
        "strcmp()", "malloc()", "printf()", or some other arbitrary
        library call.  In my blatantly biased opinion (IMBBO),
        anyone in the computer fields will benefit from grokking
        what system calls are and how they are handled in a
        multi-user environment.
             This seminar will start off with an overview of how your
        process runs when it is not invoking a system call.  Then,
        this seminar will show what occurs when your process invokes a
        system call.  From there, the seminar will explore the various
        functions performed by system calls.  And, if time permits, this
        seminar will give an overview of how virtual memory fits in to
        the picture.
             The slides used during the presentation are avaliable
        at URL: http://www.csh.rit.edu/~pat/osIntro

	*Please Note*
	This is a repeat of week 1's seminar, so that it can 
	recorded.

Location:
        Rochester Institute of Technology, Henrietta Campus.
	The seminar will be held in room A-400, in the basement
	of the Wallace library.
        For personalized directions, send email to the contact below.

Contact:   The email contact for more information, directions,
           comments or if you would like to be a guest speaker
           is adamf@csh.rit.edu.

URL:       The URL with this a schedule of seminars is:
                   URL: http://www.csh.rit.edu/os-seminars



