Dear All,

I would like to announce the release of tkxcd 1.1.0.

Tkxcd is a free diff front end that has a look and feel similar to
Atria Software's(C) xcleardiff.

Changes from 1.0.1:

   This release consist mostly of bug fixes and minor
   enhancements.  I wanted to get these out before I really
   started hacking the code.  I would recommend that you
   upgrade. The changes are listed below. (Taken from the 
   HISTORY file).

   Fix Bug where you can Edit the text areas and made
   it an option.

   Made Editable text areas a option (was a bug).

   Change Identical File bug in the Prev and Next Diff
   buttons, causing tkxcd to crash.

   Package in RPM format as well.
   Thanks to Michael J. Long.

   Make colors on left side configurable on or off.

   Fix bug where in rcs mode a file was named but no 
   version was specified it would crash.  Now it 
   diffs against the last version.

   Add description to docs of the interface for people
   who don't know xcleardiff

   Fixed the Completely Different file bug.
   (insert line at top of file bug)

Description:
 
   This program is a graphical diff front end which displays
   two files side by side highlighting in different colors the
   additions (green), deletions (red), and changes (blue)
   between the old file and the new file. It also has next and
   previous diff buttons to allow you to quickly scroll through
   the changes.  Tkxcd also has support for RCS files.


Requirements: 

   This program is based on tcl/tk.  It has been tested with
   Tck 7.4 and 7.5 with Tk 4.0 and 4.1.  I don't know if it
   works on a Mac or Windows but if somebody has a chance to
   test it on these platforms let me know how it goes.

Licensing:

   This program is free software protected under the GNU 
   General Public License (GPL).

Problems, Suggestions, Bug Reports:
  
   Also, if you have and bugs, suggestions, or other comments
   please let me know.

Location:

        http://www.doitnow.com/~quillan/john/tkxcd


Thanks and Enjoy,

John C. Quillan
