        The Linux OPaC Project - GUI & Dynamic Edition
        ==============================================

OPaC is a C++ class library which provides a complete portable
graphical user interface toolkit, providing widgets such as
buttons, check boxes, scroll bars, menus, etc.

The GUI can be edited and modified while the application is
running thanks to its dynamic user interface editor (kind of
Interface Builder). The connections between the GUI and the
application's methods can be modified at run-time too.

OPaC currently provides a platform independent access to OS
resources such as memory, files, networking, Internet access,
window management and graphism -- some are only partially
implemented. We hope that OPaC will evolve into a completely
portable application framework.

The GUI look & feel is similar to that of Win95, but a look
manager allows the implementation of various aspects.

OPaC includes features borrowed from Objective C (such as run-
time or dynamic message passing, dynamic class allocation, etc.)
and from Java (no pointers, reference count, automatic memory
deallocation, garbage collection can be added easily).

Please note that this project is new for the Linux platform.
The current sources have been tested on Win32 only and we are
looking for developers who would want to join in and help us
porting OPaC to Linux (and possibly other platforms too).

The primary Web site is http://lamicounter.epfl.ch/OPaC/ which
contains more information about the OPaC project. A description
of the dynamic user interface editor can be found there too.




