Announcing the official lauch of the most complete and intuitive 
software map and Linux reference:  http://www.linuxnow.com. 

This web site was designed and programmed by students at Caltech to 
provide comprehensive access to Linux related information.  In 
particular, it contains the best searchable and browsable software 
map based on the sunsite archive.  The site has been available to the 
Linux community for the past month and we now officially present it 
in its completed form.

Here are some key features of this site:

A Huge File Library
   o  The Linux Now file library contains over 3800 file entries 
         (1200 more than the current Linux software map!)
   o  The library is automatically updated every day by querying
         sunsite.  This produces a current and relevant database
	 of the contents of the archive.
   o  The library has a very intuitive and effecient design that
         allows users to browse through 203 categories or search the
         entire archive for specific strings.
   o  Full descriptions of each archived file are included (if these
         descriptions exist).
   o  Each file entry contains active links to seven different mirror
         sites throughout the world.  This insures fast download time.
   o  Files are screened to generate a category of all resources added
         in the last 21 days.

The Linux Forum
   o  An interactive knowledge base and technical support area in 
         which new and experinced users alike can pose questions to
         the community.
   o  The knowledge base is permament; meaning if you ask a quesion,
         it will remain on the site until it is answered.

Complete Documentation
   o  Linux Now contains an extensive catalog of Linux documentation
         including HOWTO's, FAQ's, mini-FAQ's, and info-sheets.
   o  The archive is fully indexed, categorized, cross-referenced,
         and searchable.  It is the most efficient way to find and view 
         Linux Documentation.

Benchmark Comparisons
   o  Linux Now contains an archive of benchmark results obtained
         using the BYTE Unix benchmark program and the BYTE
         Native Mode benchmark program.  Users can submit
         the results of their machine to the archive and have them
         immediately posted.

..plus much more!
   o  Linux Now is devoted to presenting the Linux community with
         information that both new and experienced users find helpful.
         This includes installation instruction, information about Linux
         vendors, and the best software available for Linux.


Visit the most exciting collection of Linux resources available on
the Web:  http://www.linuxnow.com.  

Linux Now has been already been recognized by thousands of
users around the world as the most well presented, complete, and
intuitive interface to the myriad of Linux related information 
currently available.

R. Johnson
Architect, http://www.linuxnow.com
webmaster@linuxnow.com




