                 ESSEX LINUX USERS GROUP UK MEETING 22nd MARCH 
                 =============================================

   The Essex Linux Users Group are pleased to announce that their third 
   meeting, (the first of 1997), will take place on Saturday 22nd March 
   at the offices of Brendata in Laindon, Basildon, Essex.

   Details
   =======

   Date:  Saturday 22nd March
   Time:  10:00 to 16:00
   Host:  Steve Hanselman (shanselman@brendata.co.uk)
   Place: Brendata (UK) Ltd
          Astra House,
          Christy Way,
          Southfields,
          Laindon,
          Essex,  SS15 6TQ
   Notes: This is a no-smoking building.  Smokers will have to do so
          outside.

   Agenda
   ======

   The doors will open at 10.00 and the first hour set aside for general 
   chit-chat and the setting up of a local network (10baseT/2) by those who 
   bring along their PC's, before the meeting formally gets under way at 1100.
   
   A brief opening speech by Geoff Blake will be followed by a presentation 
   on Perl by Alec Clews and after a suitable recess will continue with a 
   talk about Linux in the workplace entitled, "Linux: Office Applications", 
   by Clive Messer.

   After a break for lunch at a local pub, Peter Onion, (who gave the
   excellent presentation on the version 2.X.X kernels at ELUG-1), will be 
   talking about Visual Tk/Tcl - the Linux answer to Visual Basic. 

   Running as a parallel stream to the presentations will be an Installfest.
   On hand will be facilities and assistance to install or upgrade Linux on 
   your PC  via NFS,  FTP or  CDROM.  It is  intended to  have most popular 
   distributions   available  and  possibly  a  direct  connection  to  the 
   Internet.

   Finally,  the meeting will be concluded with a draw. One lucky person
   will return home with a full copy of Applix office suite thanks to the 
   kind folks at RedHat.

   Directions
   ==========

*  Take the A127 (the 2nd junction north of the Dartford Tunnel on the
   M25) east towards Southend.
*  Take the Southfields turnoff (just after the petrol garage on the other
   carriageway).
*  Turn right at the roundabout over the A127 (do not take the Ford
   entrance!)
*  Follow the bend to the next roundabout by Toomeys Garage, and turn left
*  Go over the next mini-roundabout.
*  At the end of the road, Astra House is the building ahead of you to
   the right.
*  Parking is available either in the car park behind the building or in
   front of the building.

   Further Information
   ===================

   Please send email to elug@palaemon.demon.co.uk if you require any further 
   assistance.

   Many thanks to RedHat Software Inc for the Applixware package and to
   Steve Hanselman for making the premises available.

   ========================================================================

   Essex Linux User Group is a loosely formed group of Linux enthusiasts in
   primarily the South-East of England.  Meetings are open to all those who 
   have any interest in Linux,  a *free* clone of the UNIX operating system
   or those who just wish to come along and see what all the fuss is about. 
   
   The Linux  kernel itself  is the result of  international collaboration, 
   directed by  Linus Torvalds  the original author,  by enthusiasts on the 
   Internet. For more details of Linux see http://www.linux.org 



Geoff
