.

  Hello all,

  This is to announce the release of xisp version 1.3, an X11 visual
 interface to pppd/chat, in other words, an X11 dialup networking
 tool for Linux. The .lsm entry and part of the README file is included
 below. Everything is in sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming right now
 but it should appear in its proper location shortly.

  Changes from version 1.2 include: support for automatic redialing
 per ISP entry of a dropped connection if desired, support for a user
 customizable modem initialization string for xispdial, and of course
 a few bug fixes :). The user interface has been enhanced somewhat,
 now also displaying the selected ISP on the main window. Since some
 minor changes were made to the .xisprc file format, a utility is
 provided for users to convert v1.2 .xisprc files to v1.3; just run
 the xisprccv utility with no arguments.

  Please send bug reports/enhancements to dbouras@hol.gr. With hope
 that you'll have as much fun with it as I did coding it, and with
 greetings from sunny Athens, Greece,

  Dimitri

