Jcd 1.1, a Java Audio CD Player, is now available for Linux and SGI
IRIX.
   Pre-compiled Linux-ix86/IRIX binary with full source at:
        http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/jcd-1.1.tar.gz
        http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/jcd-1.1.tar.gz
   Final destination:
        http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/apps/sound/cds/jcd-1.1.tar.gz
   Screen shots
        http://www.actrix.gen.nz/users/michael/giveaways.html

In case you need a Java Development Kit, free kits can be found here:
   Linux:  http://www.blackdown.org/java-linux.html
   IRIX:   http://www.sgi.com/Fun/free/web-tools.html

Jcd is really just an experiment in building things with Java, so
don't expect a polished commercial effort and you won't be disappointed.
Some of the objects may be of interest to Java developers, eg
gif-buttons,
cddb client.

Jcd is an application, not an applet, ie it accesses files and
devices and can't be run under Netscape.  You must use something that
runs a Java application: eg Sun's JDK.  If you've managed to get the
AWT to run, you shouldn't have any trouble installing and running jcd.

Features in 1.0:
  - Play/Stop/Pause/Prev/Next/Eject/Volume control panel.
  - Track/Index direct access by entry into the numeric display.
  - Displays track, index, num-tracks,
track-time/track-remaining/disc-rem'ing.
  - Program play, continuous/single play, shuffle play.
  - Xmcd CDDB artist/disc/track title lookup and display.
    - Xmcd CDDB database format and protocols courtesy of Ti Kan and
      Steve Scherf (http://sunsite.unc.edu/~cddb/xmcd).
    - Optional remote CDDB server lookup.
    - Autosave of remote lookups to local cache.
    - GUI window for creating/editing artist/title/track local cache
entries.
  - Icon button widget - e.g. play button, pause button light up when
active.
  - Penguin button (ie plug for Linux).

Features added in jcd 1.1:
  - A minor upgrade from 1.0.
  - Auto load of appropriate native module, i.e. use the same
installation
    for all supported platforms.
  - All windows now respond to close requests.
    Thanks to Randy Chapman <chapman@u.washington.edu>
  - Reduced reservation of memory in the jcd starup script.
    Thanks also to Randy Chapman.
  - Added Add/Delete/Play mode to the program window.
  - Main window now sets its icon.
  - SGI IRIX support
    - Uses the SGI cdaudio library => output to drive headphone socket
only.
    - Volume control doesn't work under IRIX (why?).
    - Index play and index display doesn't work under IRIX cdaudio
(how?).
                      
