FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE

INTERNET ADVERTISERS HOP ONTO FREE LILYPAD SOFTWARE

CHICAGO - With the Web ad industry expected to hit US$2 billion in 1997,
effective advertising response measurement is becoming an increasingly hot
topic.

With just that topic in mind, Streams Online Media Development today
announces the public release of Lilypad, the only tool developed
exclusively for internet marketers to measure and assess response to their
online media buys and promotional efforts.

Lilypad 1.9b1 is available for free download and 60-day trial at
http://www.lilypad.net/

"The new version of Lilypad is leaps and bounds ahead of our 1995 release.
We've been carefully studying how our clients use Lilypad, and we've
implemented many of their suggestions. Lilypad is now available to everyone
for a variety of operating systems," says Streams president Dave Skwarczek.
"and for now, it's free."

Until now, the only measurable data available to Web marketers was found in
their server's access logs. Since Lilypad generates its own data, internet
marketers now have access to previously unavailable information.

Developed in accordance with the CASIE Guidelines for Interactive Media
Measurement, Lilypad is the only package that allows internet media buyers
to make informed decisions.

That's because Lilypad offers marketers the ability to measure
clickthroughs across all ad buys in all web media and ad networks. This
makes it possible to measure trends in response to banner ads and online
promotional efforts.

Lilypad also lets marketers determine whose Web pages, search engines,
newsgroups and intranet pages are linked to their Web site, and measure
when and how many visitors jump to their site using those links. Lilypad
also measures bookmarks and direct accesses. This enables web marketers to
effectively measure the results of their online promotional campaigns.

"Lilypad is a unique, powerful and important tool for marketers. Though it
has been a visible player in the tracking industry, it has only been
available to our consulting clients. We received so much positive response
from the industry that we're convinced everyone should have a copy,"
concludes Dominic Tassone, Lilypad product manager.

Streams Online Media Development is an internet development studio
providing content development, design, programming and marketing services.
Streams serves Fortune 500 clients and other progressive organizations
seeking to create online presences with effect, meaning and power.

