The Rutgers University Student Linux Users Group (RU-SLUG) will hold
its next general meeting on Wednesday, March 5, 1997, at 9:30 PM in
Hill Center Room 116 on the Busch Campus of Rutgers University.

After normal business, a talk entitled "Writing Linux Character Device
Drivers" will be presented by member Tom Dyas. Tom will discuss how to
write a bare-bones character device driver as well as provide a brief
overiew of writing modules (the driver has to get into the kernel
somehow :) ).

A question and answer session will follow.

Directions to the meeting can be found off the RU-SLUG homepage at
<URL:http://www-slug.rutgers.edu/>.



