Excerpt from dlq/README:

dlq 0.50 - download queue
- -------------------------

dlq is a simple queueing, anonymous download service that runs as lines are
idle.  It is meant for slow serial devices (i.e. modems), where large
transfers can completely inhibit other activity.  It is written in perl.

Usage
- -----

A server runs 'dlqd', which sends files located in user "spool" directories
to clients.  Their paths look like ~user/spool.
[...]

Client machines run 'dlqrecvd' which retrieves data when the local pipe is
idle.  The files are deposited in a shared directory, usually
/usr/local/spool or somesuch.
[...]

'qadd' adds requests to the client queue.  If joe (username also joe) has
some files on the server, ~joe/spool/afile and ~joe/spool/bfile, he can
queue them for receipt with
    # qadd joe/afile joe/bfile
or if he likes perl regular expressions, with
    # qadd -e "joe/\wfile"
The files will subsequently appear in /usr/local/spool.
[...]

- -jeremy



