Etherboot-3.0 is a package containing code that can be put in a NIC
PROM to boot Linux diskless using bootp, tftp and/or NFS.

A few changes have been made since 3.0b2, mostly by Markus Gutschke,
please see the LOG for details of all the changes since 2.1; there are
too many to list here. Netboot-0.5 is included in the package; this
also includes construction information for a Flash EPROM ISA card.

If you intend to swap over NFS you will need to apply Claus Heine's
contributed patches to a 2.0.x kernel.

It has been uploaded into ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/incoming/Linux and
should show up at mirrors everywhere soon, normally in the
system/Linux-boot directory. In the meantime it is also available from
ftp://ftp.syd.dit.csiro.au/pub/ken/etherboot-3.0.{tar.gz,lsm}.

        Ken

