Greetings,

I've been playing around making my linux box into an audio signal
generator, capable of generating sine, cosine, square, sawtooth, triangle,
pulse, noise waves at a resolution of 1 hertz. There is 'sgen' a command
line generator, and 'siggen' an Ncurses based generator. There's also yet
another command line mixer 'smix', and 'soundinfo' which interrogates the
kernel, and describes many of the /dev/mixer and /dev/dsp features
available.

I'd like to do a generator using svgalib and have a fancy mouse driven
front interface etc, but I haven't the time. I'm working on some
alternative generation techniques, so that I can do a sweep generator
and be able to do fourier synthesis of waveforms and other stuff, like two
tone test signals etc.


