-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


I'm releasing my first verion of libaio, a library containing the
asynchronous I/O routines from POSIX.1b. Here's the README  file:

		 libaio - An Asynchronous I/O Library

	This is an attempt to write a POSIX.1b compliant library for
the necessary asynchronous I/O functions. So far I've been able to
implement the following functions:

	aio_cancel
	aio_fsync
	aio_read
	aio_write
	lio_list

The function aio_suspend is waiting while I decide what's the best way
to implement it. Suggestions are encouraged.

Caveats
- -------

	So far I've only tested this library with the following:

		Linux kernel 2.0.27, libc-5.3.12, linuxthreads-0.5

You must have some POSIX thread library to compile this library, but
I'm not sure if other's will work.

	To make lio_list work, I use signal SIGUSR2 internally. This
might cause you problems if you use it elsewhere.

	I've defined an additional error code, ECANCELED, that seems
to be required.

	I'll admit that I'm guessing as to how close this is to POSIX
compliance, as I don't have the specs in house.

Building
- --------

	Please examine the makefile & make changes as needed, then do
a 'make'.

Testing
- -------
	'make tests' creates some simple test programs.

Installing
- ----------
	Once you decide to keep libaio, install it as root via 'make
install'. 

Documentation
- -------------

	None yet, that should be in the next release.
	
